name: Hideout Furniture — Runtime Editor and Workbench
author: Hardcoon
version: 0.5.91
description: Shared IX-Ray editor, Hideout Furniture 2.3.2, Expansion 1.0.2, Even More Hideout Furniture Update 2, native QA doors and portable repair, upgrade and crafting workbench. 212 furniture items, three portable campfires with native lighting transitions, cooking and seven edible cooked meats, paired door placement actions, modes 1/2/3 with fixed preview, remembered Q display styles, R rotation axes and 15-metre placement, translucent previews, unlimited lights, NPC doors and 1.4-second Use pickup. Stock first wave adds 28 inventory items and 37 placement visuals using original game OGF/DDS references, grouped tools and five fence variants.; bare bulb with compact collision and 6 m light. Portable primus with standard gas-lamp light/audio and an animated sliding door reuse original game OGF models. Seven selected map props reuse original game textures; piano and bunk bed remain decorative. Nine further map props reuse original game textures. Three final selected props add a walkable plank deck, reel radio and green crate group. Map furniture fronts and pivots are normalized, collision follows fitted parts and tooltips match the common furniture layout. Map armchair113, grey sofa114 and motor160 are removed by user request. Rejected map props are removed; the complete closed sandbag object is restored from both level draw calls. Savka stocks the wide plank deck in lots of ten and keeps both refrigerators in storage. Cable reel removed; sandbags are construction materials stocked five each. Cargo container remains available in the game but is not sold by Savka. Map refrigerator inventory icon is2x3 cells; light sofa is3x2.
